{"name":"Pirouette","hex":"#f9e4e9","fetched":"2026-10-18","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pirouette","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A whirling or turning on the toes in dancing, primarily in ballet.","The whirling about of a horse."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To perform a pirouette; to whirl on the toes, like a dancer."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pirouette"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pirouette (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Pirouette is the second studio album by the American noise rock and dance-punk band Model/Actriz. Released on May 2, 2025, by the independent record label True Panther Sounds, the album has been widely praised by music critics. The lead single \"Cinderella\" was released on February 25, 2025, as a teaser, followed by the singles \"Doves\" and \"Diva\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4f/Pirouette_%28album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pirouette_(album)","wikidata":"Q134470386"},{"title":"Pirouette (dressage)","blocks":[{"text":"A pirouette is a two-track lateral movement asked of a horse in dressage, in which the animal makes a circle with its front end around a smaller circle made by the hind end. Specifically, the front legs and outside hind leg should travel around the inside hind leg, with the horse remaining slightly bent in the direction of travel. From the part of the rider it needs \"much practice in collecting and balancing the horse and in using the aids correctly.\"\nThe horse may perform the movement at the walk or canter, although the pirouette at the walk is more commonly called the turn on the haunches. It \"can also be executed at piaffe.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/AztecaHorse.jpg/330px-AztecaHorse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pirouette_(dressage)","wikidata":"Q1759562"},{"title":"Turn (dance and gymnastics)","blocks":[{"text":"In dance and gymnastics, a turn is a rotation of the body about the vertical axis. It is usually a complete rotation of the body, although quarter (90°) and half (180°) turns are possible for some types of turns. Multiple, consecutive turns are typically named according to the number of 360° rotations."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Flamenco_Dancer_2_%285514546691%29.jpg/330px-Flamenco_Dancer_2_%285514546691%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turn_(dance_and_gymnastics)","wikidata":"Q7855632"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/4f/Pirouette_%28album%29.jpg/250px-Pirouette_%28album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4f/Pirouette_%28album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/4f/Pirouette_%28album%29.jpg/250px-Pirouette_%28album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APirouette_(album).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Model_Actriz_live_%28cropped%29.png/500px-Model_Actriz_live_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Model_Actriz_live_%28cropped%29.png/1280px-Model_Actriz_live_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Model_Actriz_live_%28cropped%29.png/500px-Model_Actriz_live_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Model/Actriz performing live in 2023. Left to right: Jack Wetmore, Cole Haden, Ruben Radlauer, Aaron Shapiro.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AModel_Actriz_live_(cropped).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/AztecaHorse.jpg/500px-AztecaHorse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/AztecaHorse.jpg/1280px-AztecaHorse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/AztecaHorse.jpg/500px-AztecaHorse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Beginning of a canter pirouette to the right.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAztecaHorse.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Annabellecollins.jpg/500px-Annabellecollins.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Annabellecollins.jpg/500px-Annabellecollins.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Canter pirouette to the left. The horse has transferred its center of gravity towards the hind quarters. Its hind legs are then raised and lowered almost in the same place in the canter rhythm.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnnabellecollins.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Flamenco_Dancer_2_%285514546691%29.jpg/500px-Flamenco_Dancer_2_%285514546691%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Flamenco_Dancer_2_%285514546691%29.jpg/1280px-Flamenco_Dancer_2_%285514546691%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Flamenco_Dancer_2_%285514546691%29.jpg/500px-Flamenco_